.TH DANBY-PROJECTILE 1
.SH NAME
danby-projectile \- a plain projectile with drag
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/projectile
.SH MODEL
The unflavoured projectile, as against the sixteen sport-specific models
beside it: no bat, no ball, no wind, just
.IR ballistics (2)'s
own acceleration exposed directly.  Speed, launch angle, drag, lift, spin
and gravity are the parameters, and the same
.B acceleration()
the sports models call is what integrates them.
.SH DISPLAY
The spatial graph shows the flight path; telemetry shows speed.  Tracks
change every parameter live.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/projectile.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby (1),
.IR trajlab (2),
.IR ballistics (2)
.SH BUGS
The model is deliberately state-independent in its aerodynamics: drag and
lift coefficients are constants, not functions of Reynolds number, so it
does not reproduce the drag crisis that the sport models paper over with
per-sport coefficients either.
